Steps:
[NAV] Go to Store details for {{STORE_ID}}
[ACT] Enter Store URL in field: {{FRONT_URL}}
[ACT] Save changes
[ACT] Click Open in Browser button

Assertions:
[DOM] with store:access only, the Stores menu item is visible and the Stores blade opens {OBSERVED}
[API] with store:access only, POST /api/stores/search returns 403 {DOC} -- access opens a module, read is needed to view its data (VirtoOZ permission model: *:access vs *:read; vc-module-store StoreModuleController.SearchStores requires StoreAuthorizationRequirement(store:read))
[DOM] with store:access only, the Stores blade lists no stores {OBSERVED}
[API] with store:access + store:read, POST /api/stores/search returns 200 and the results include {{STORE_ID}} {DOC}
[DOM] with store:access + store:read, the Stores blade lists {{STORE_ID}} {OBSERVED}

Steps:
[NAV] Login as User_1 at {{BACK_URL}}
[NAV] Open Stores > Select Store_1
[ACT] Make changes to store settings

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[API] PUT /api/stores as User_1 returns 204 for the permitted store; the change is visible on GET /api/stores/{id}
[CONSOLE] No 403 on store endpoints (/api/stores...); 403 from the store blade's SEO and dynamic-property widgets is expected for this role and is not asserted
[ADMIN] Changes saved and reflected for User_1

Steps:
[NAV] Login as Admin at {{BACK_URL}}
[NAV] Navigate to Security > Users > User_1
[ACT] Click Login on Behalf
[API] GET {{BACK_URL}}/api/platform/security/users/{{ADMIN_EMAIL}} as Admin and capture the account e-mail as admin_account_email ({{ADMIN_EMAIL}} holds the admin USERNAME on some envs, not the e-mail)
[ACT] If the storefront shows a Security verification page, re-enter admin_account_email and {{ADMIN_PASSWORD}}; the username alone keeps the verification button disabled
[ASSERT] Verify logged in as User_1 on Storefront at {{FRONT_URL}}

Assertions:
[STATE] Stores.IsSpa = false after Save, confirmed by the API read-back {OBSERVED}
[NETWORK] navigating by menu and product clicks issues no new document request — routes change client-side and data comes from GraphQL {OBSERVED} -- vc-frontend is always a single-page app; xAPI StoreSettings.IsSpa is marked obsolete, so the setting has no storefront effect
[DOM] the category and product pages render normally with Is SPA off {OBSERVED}
